--- Tony Plate <tplate at blackmesacapital.com> wrote:
> Include the adjustment in your derivative so that it
> is correct wrt to your 
> adjusted objective.  Then the solver will "see" it. 
> This is known as 
> reparameterization and is a common and effective
> technique -- it replaces a 
> constrained optimization by a less constrained one. 
> The only tricky part 
> here is to ensure that the sum of weights is > 0. 
> If it is possible to 
> have all weights strictly greater than zero, then
> consider the transform w 
> = exp(x) / sum(exp(x)), where x (a vector) is
> completely unconstrained, and 
> w is a vector of positive weights that sums to 1.
> 
> hope this helps,
> 
> Tony Plate
