Dear all

I have a list consisting of about 20 sublists, each representing 
observations (where each observation has some structure, therefore 
the list) on an individual. Each sublist is quite large, about 10 MB. I 
have them collected in a list because this allows me to do analysis 
on the single time series by stepping through the list.

But: this gets quite slow. I therefore consider to store each sublist as 
an single object. Is there a way to work with each element of a set of  
objects, something like 
        for (i in sublist1,sublist2,sublist3) 
where i gets assigned the sublists consecutively? Or any other trick?

Thanks for a hint, Wolfgang Bauer

